# Investigation Ethics

OSINTGraph handles potentially sensitive personal data. All development must respect these boundaries.

## Allowed

- Public profiles and pages
- Data voluntarily entered by the analyst
- Official APIs with proper credentials
- Manual observation with documented source
- Import from analyst-owned exports (CSV, JSON)

## Forbidden — never implement

- Authentication bypass or session theft
- Access to private or locked accounts
- Credential stuffing or password attacks
- Platform protection bypass (CAPTCHA farms, anti-bot evasion)
- Automated stalking or harassment tooling
- Deanonymization presented as certainty without public evidence

## Data handling

- Preserve uncertainty: use confidence scores and status labels
- Distinguish observation (fact seen) from hypothesis (interpretation)
- AI suggestions require analyst Confirm / Reject / Mark for review
- Entity resolution creates Merge Suggestions only — never auto-merge persons

## Connector capabilities

Display acquisition method clearly: MANUAL, PUBLIC_SEARCH, OFFICIAL_API, IMPORT.

Do not simulate capabilities that do not exist legally or technically.

## Logging

Never log emails, phone numbers, session tokens, or raw API keys.
